          "heading": "Bill Sweeney confirms WRU's formal request for Welsh clubs to join Prem",
          "body": "The Welsh Rugby Union wants its clubs in English rugby's top flight, and the RFU has confirmed the request. Speaking to BBC Radio Four, chief executive Bill Sweeney said the RFU had \"received a formal approach\" and must go back with more questions. Its stated focus remains expanding the English game, with the Premiership moving from 10 to 12 clubs. The United Rugby Championship has threatened the WRU, a shareholder, with legal action over leaving."
